===Verb===
{{de-verb|ab.fahren<fährt#fuhr,gefahren,führe.haben,sein>}}

# {{lb|de|intransitive|auxiliary {{m|de|sein}}}} to [[depart]], to [[leave]]
#: {{ux|de|Ihr Zug '''fährt''' um fünf Uhr '''ab.'''|Her train departs at 5 o'clock.}}
#: {{ux|de|Wir werden morgen '''abfahren.'''|We will '''leave''' tomorrow}}
# {{lb|de|transitive|auxiliary {{m|de|haben}}}} to [[carry off]], to [[remove]]
#: {{ux|de|Der Müll wird zweimal pro Woche '''abgefahren'''.|The garbage is '''picked up''' twice a week.}}
# {{lb|de|intransitive|with {{m|de|auf}}|auxiliary {{m|de|sein}}|idiomatic|colloquial}} to [[go for]]; to be [[crazy]] about, for; to be a [[fan]] of or [[infatuated]] with
#: {{ux|de|Sie '''fährt''' voll auf Kultfilme '''ab.'''|She''''s''' really '''crazy about''' cult movies.}}
# {{lb|de|transitive|auxiliary {{m|de|sein}} or {{m|de|haben}}}} to [[drive]] [[along]] {{q|a stretch of road in search of something}}; to [[patrol]]
#: {{ux|de|
Lass uns die Strecke noch mal '''abfahren''', vielleicht finden wir ihn doch.|Let's '''drive along''' this stretch of road again, we might still find him}}
# to [[wear down]] {{q|tyres}}
# to [[use up]] {{q|all one's journeys on a travel card}}
# to [[knock off]] {{q|something by hitting it with one's vehicle}}
# {{lb|de|jemanden abfahren lassen|vulgar}} to send someone packing; to tell someone to go away
